From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 22:43:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] media: cedrus: vc1: reject Main profile intensity
 compensation

The H6 video engine has a hardware limitation: Main/WMV3 profile with
intensity compensation (MVMODE=4) produces accumulating drift on every
P-frame.  The vendor BSP (TvdVideo) blocks all Main/WMV3 content at
the application level; the kernel allowed it but produced broken output
(pinball 12.5 dB, factory 17.3 dB, snowboard 13.5 dB).

Main profile without IC works correctly (Robotica_720, SMM0015, etc.
are bit-exact).

Reject only Main+IC frames at the V4L2 control-validation level so
that ffmpeg falls back to software decode instead of producing
drifting garbage.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Developed-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>

[Ported to the VC-1 stateless uAPI revision 3 (gus bourg): the profile
and MVMODE are now in two controls. The check moves to the picture layer
control and reads the profile from the current value of the sequence
control, which FFmpeg sets when the decoder is opened (and with every
request). As before, the picture is refused when it is queued; FFmpeg
cannot switch to software in the middle of a stream, so such a stream
fails rather than falling back. The misleading indentation of the
original (-Wmisleading-indentation) is gone.]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
index 1d30fbfd4..d483b0ee0 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.c
@@ -95,6 +95,18 @@ static int cedrus_try_ctrl(struct v4l2_ctrl *ctrl)
 	} else if (ctrl->id == V4L2_CID_STATELESS_VC1_PICTURE_LAYER) {
 		const struct v4l2_ctrl_vc1_picture_layer *pic =
 			ctrl->p_new.p_vc1_picture_layer;
+		struct cedrus_ctx *ctx = container_of(ctrl->handler, struct cedrus_ctx, hdl);
+		const struct v4l2_ctrl_vc1_sequence *seq;
+
+		/*
+		 * Main profile intensity compensation drifts on the H6 video
+		 * engine. The profile is in the sequence control, which is set
+		 * before the pictures (at the latest with the first one).
+		 */
+		seq = cedrus_find_control_data(ctx, V4L2_CID_STATELESS_VC1_SEQUENCE);
+		if (seq && seq->profile == V4L2_VC1_PROFILE_MAIN &&
+		    pic->mvmode == V4L2_VC1_MVMODE_INTENSITY_COMP)
+			return -EINVAL;
 
 		if (pic->respic)
 			/* Reduced-resolution (multi-res) coding is not supported */
